        "math_academy_id": "q-171017",
        "problem": "$\\,$ $7=5$ or $-3\\ge 0.$\n\nWhat is the negation of the compound statement above?",
        "worked_solution": "De Morgan's law for disjunctions states that the negation of a disjunction of two statements is equivalent to the conjunction of the negations of the individual statements. It can be stated symbolically as follows:\n\n$$\n\u00ac(A\u2228B)=\u00acA\u2227\u00acB\n$$\n\nSo, the negation of our statement is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u00ac(7=5\\text{\u00a0or\u00a0}-3\\ge 0) & \u2261\u00ac((7=5)\u2228(-3\\ge 0)) \\\\  & \u2261\u00ac(7=5)\u2227\u00ac(-3\\ge 0) \\\\  & \u2261(7\\ne 5)\u2227(-3<0) \\\\  & \u22617\\ne 5\\text{\u00a0and\u00a0}-3<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        "actual_result": "Correct",
        "deliberately_incorrect_submission": false,
        "submitted_fields": [
          {
            "key": "selection",
            "submitted_value": "$7\\ne 5$ and $-3<0$",
            "submitted_option": "e",
            "observed_selected_option": "e"
          }
        ]
      }
